Attributes.description:
Recognition Status indicates how receiving organisations or systems may acknowledge, interpret, or display an individual’s self‑identified nationality, country, or group in operational systems or reporting.&#x20;

It captures organisational handling rules (e.g. approved, restricted, suppressed) applied to a self‑reported identity that has no legal standing but is relevant to inclusion, engagement, or user experience.&#x20;

Values should be drawn from a controlled vocabulary rather than free text, to ensure consistency and interoperability.&#x20;

This represents how the self‑identified value is handled in practice, not whether a state or international body formally recognises the group.

